course: dictionary
lesson: 13194
title: What does ft mean?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: ft is the short form of foot or feet. A foot is a unit of length, which means a way to measure how long, wide, or tall something is. We write ft instead of writing the whole word.
explain: One foot is 12 inches, and it is about 30 centimetres. So 3 ft is the same as 1 yard. «The shelf is 3 ft long» tells you the shelf is about one metre long.
explain: The words around ft tell you what it measures. «She is 5 ft 4 in tall» means she is 5 feet and 4 inches tall. «The room is 10 ft wide» tells you how wide the room is. Square ft, written sq ft, measures area, the space covered by a flat surface.
fact: ft is short for foot (one) and feet (more than one).
fact: 1 ft = 12 inches, about 30 centimetres.
fact: 1 yard = 3 ft.
fact: Heights are often given in feet and inches, for example «5 ft tall», especially in the USA, and also in the UK and Canada.
fact: In song titles, «ft.» can mean «featuring», and «Ft» can be short for «Fort», as in Ft Worth.
exercise: «The door is 7 ft high.» What does ft stand for? | inches | *feet | kilometres | grams
exercise: How many inches are in 1 ft? | 10 | 6 | 30 | *12
exercise: 1 yard is the same as how many ft? | 4 | *3 | 2 | 12
test: «The kitchen ceiling is 8 ft high.» Roughly how tall is that in centimetres? | about 800 cm | about 30 cm | *about 240 cm | about 8 cm
test: «She is 5 ft 4 in tall.» What does 5 ft mean? | 5 metres | 5 yards | *5 feet | 5 inches
exam: A garden is 10 ft long and 6 ft wide. What is its area in square ft? | 600 sq ft | 16 sq ft | *60 sq ft | 30 sq ft
